WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.320
Hydrogen burns in oxygen to make water. Write it down: H two plus O two gives H two O. Count the atoms. Did an atom just vanish?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.240
Count the oxygen atoms on each side. Which side is short?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:36.340
Left: two oxygen atoms. Right: only one. But atoms are never created or destroyed in a reaction. That is the law of conservation of mass. So each element needs the same count on both sides.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:48.660
Put a two in front of water. Oxygen: two and two. Hydrogen is four on the right, so put a two in front of hydrogen. Four and four. Balanced.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:59.180
Why not write H two O two? That is hydrogen peroxide, a different substance. Change the coefficients in front, never the subscripts inside.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:06.500
Atoms are conserved, so count every element on both sides, and balance with coefficients only.

